            "parity_status": "covered_differently",
            "excludable": true,
            "rationale": "Both are about a constraint that validates existing rows while holding a lock. SQLens reasons about the NOT VALID / VALIDATE split for constraints generally rather than foreign keys specifically, so the ground is the same and the shape is not.",
            "source_url": "https://squawkhq.com/docs/rules/adding-foreign-key-constraint"
        },
